---
description: JavaScript hard bans (subset of TypeScript rules).
globs: **/*.js,**/*.jsx,**/*.mjs,**/*.cjs
alwaysApply: false
---

- NEVER: `var`, `==`/`!=`, `new Buffer()`, `Function()`, `require()` in `.mjs`, `import` in `.cjs`, callback-style Node APIs when a Promise variant exists.
- ALWAYS: `const`/`let`, `===`/`!==`, `Buffer.from(...)`, `node:fs/promises`.
- NEVER `catch (e) {}`. Log structured context and rethrow a domain `Error` with `cause:`.
- TODO/FIXME require `TODO(@owner, TICKET-123)`. Prefer migrating to TypeScript (see `11-typescript-style.mdc`).
